The upbeat and energectic version of Mill Fever from the GBA port of DKC3, composed by Dave Wise.



24/02 Update Changed the name of the samples to make them easier to read;

A chorded variation of the rythm guitar sample was added;

Trimmed the acid bass sample to accomodate the new chorded guitar sample (and with that I mean, there was a huge portion of the sample that was not playing at all, and was eating all the ARAM. It was made more to save space than adding the new sample);

Changed some pitch bends of the harpsichord;

Increased the echo effect of the synth envelopes to sound more like the original;

Lowered the echo buffer byte by 1, to save some space on ARAM;

Switched places of the organ chord played at channel #6 on at the end of the song, to channels #2 and #4, to accomodate the chorded guitar sample that was missing before;

Lowered the master volume to w216.

An original song I made in a competition of ORG Maker. I felt so happy with what I had composed, that I wanted to port it.

I think it doesn't seem to fit very well in a SMW level, unless someone use it wisely.



03/19/2021 Update * Did rework the entire port from zero, so now every section is properly optimized, and the text file is MUCH MORE readable;

* Added more channels to fill the strings part, so it sounds much more fuller;

* Replaced the cymbal sample to the KSS one;

* Reworked on most of non Kirby samples, downgrading some, and making the organ-like wave more higher quality;

* Crammed all of the percussion parts in one single channel;

* Added a second text file which does contain the final section of the song (which is where the actual song ends, instead of looping forever). Keep in mind that the full one loops once, then it'll stay silent, like the original piece;

* Lowered the global volume to w166.



03/22/2021 Update: Just a small fix on the organ-like wave sample on the full version, where the highest note channel overflows at the final section.

